{"corpusid": 987654321, "openaccessinfo": {"externalids": {"ArXiv": "1501.00011", "DOI": null, "MAG": null, "ACL": null, "PubMedCentral": null, "Medline": null, "MedRxiv": null}, "license": "CCBY", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1501.00011", "status": "GREEN", "disclaimer": ""}, "title": "Radar Signal Denoising", "authors": ["Sara Ali"], "body": {"text": "\nIntroduction\n\nRadar signals are corrupted by clutter and thermal noise, which motivates sparse recovery methods for denoising returns in practice.\nMethods\n\nWe solve a basis pursuit problem with an orthogonal matching pursuit solver and tune the sparsity level by cross validation on held-out pulses.\nReferences\n\n[1] Some reference.", "annotations": {"section_header": "[{\"start\": 1, \"end\": 13, \"attributes\": {\"n\": \"1.\"}}, {\"start\": \"148\", \"end\": \"155\", \"attributes\": {\"n\": \"2.\"}}, {\"start\": 301, \"end\": 311, \"attributes\": null}]", "paragraph": "[{\"start\": 15, \"end\": 28, \"attributes\": null}]", "sentence": null, "bib_ref": null}}, "bibliography": {"text": "[1] Some reference.", "annotations": {"bib_entry": null}}}
